The linked resource is an archive of articles from Marc Andreessen’s blog, which includes insights on career planning and opportunities.

Most AI teams don't fail because of the model; they fail because of the data. We launched Adaptive Data to optimize your data across 242 languages. Today we're making it programmable with the Adaptive Data API and Python SDK. You can ingest, adapt, evaluate, and export with just a few calls in a few minutes.

The early deployments show an average quality improvement of 82%.

@adaption_ai: "Data optimization that used to live behind a UI now lives in your code. The Adaptive Data API and Python SDK are here. 82% average quality improvement. 242 languages. Adapt your world."

Last week, we spoke with a team scaling into six markets. Their AI worked well in English, but their users speak Brazilian Portuguese, German, and Arabic, and they want a native experience without falling back to English or producing low-quality results. Translation often leads to awkward grammar and tone, making the output feel unnatural.

This is a training data problem; if your model only learned from English-heavy data, it thinks in English, resulting in subpar outputs for other languages. Today, we're launching Expand Your World in Adaptive Data, allowing you to adapt your training data into 242 languages without a translation wrapper. Your model will think natively in your users' language, making your AI feel local everywhere it ships.

@adaption_ai: "Most datasets reflect the world as it was convenient to capture, not as it actually exists. Introducing Expand Your World, a new feature in Adaptive Data. 242 languages and localizations. The fastest way to global coverage."

